{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41699630",
      "title": "Sharing Cross-Component State When Working With Compound Components",
      "sourceHash": "f96e61caf525bdf198b0f8db956ea6267a001062737ac8341383bbd5b9011867",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.8,
          "en": "Now, there still are two last things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 6.24,
          "en": "that could be improved here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.24,
          "end": 8.58,
          "en": "regarding the accordion component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.58,
          "end": 11.7,
          "en": "And the first thing that could be improved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.7,
          "end": 13.71,
          "en": "is that we have to set that id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.71,
          "end": 15.813,
          "en": "on both the title and the content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.95,
          "end": 17.97,
          "en": "It would be nicer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.97,
          "end": 21.9,
          "en": "if we would just have to set it once on the Item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.9,
          "end": 24.96,
          "en": "and that Item would then pass it down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.96,
          "end": 27.003,
          "en": "to the Title and Content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.86,
          "end": 31.86,
          "en": "Now, we can't do that with help of props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.86,
          "end": 34.23,
          "en": "because the AccordionItem component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.23,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "which is meant to receive that id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 38.91,
          "en": "doesn't have direct access to its children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.91,
          "end": 43.08,
          "en": "It just forwards them between those list item tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 45.21,
          "en": "We're not outputting them as components here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.21,
          "end": 47.1,
          "en": "in that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.1,
          "end": 48.54,
          "en": "But we can of course, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.54,
          "end": 51.81,
          "en": "use context as a solution here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 55.62,
          "en": "We can create another piece of context here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.62,
          "end": 60.36,
          "en": "and that would be the AccordionItemContext in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.36,
          "end": 64.29,
          "en": "And here, it's a super simple local context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.29,
          "end": 67.26,
          "en": "which will only be needed by a few components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.26,
          "end": 70.89,
          "en": "that are wrapped by one specific AccordionItem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.89,
          "end": 75.21000000000001,
          "en": "So, inside of the AccordionItem component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.21000000000001,
          "end": 80.21000000000001,
          "en": "we can return AccordionItemContext.Provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.57,
          "end": 84,
          "en": "And the value I wanna provide here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "will not be dynamic at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 90.78,
          "en": "Instead, the value I wanna set on this Provider component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.78,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "will simply be that id that's received on AccordionItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.91,
          "end": 99.39,
          "en": "so that components wrapped by this AccordionItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.39,
          "end": 104.31,
          "en": "will be able to access that id through the context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 107.95,
          "en": "Now for that, I'll again add a custom hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.95,
          "end": 110.85300000000001,
          "en": "useAccordionItemContext,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.75,
          "end": 114.75,
          "en": "so that we can safely extract that context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.75,
          "end": 117.363,
          "en": "with help of the built-in useContext hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 122.73,
          "en": "using that Accordion, I had a typo there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.73,
          "end": 126.693,
          "en": "so that should be a AccordionItemContext.Proovider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.98,
          "end": 128.813,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.11,
          "end": 133.983,
          "en": "And then, using that here to select that context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135,
          "end": 136.95,
          "en": "And then, of course we wanna return it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.95,
          "end": 141.81,
          "en": "but in between, we wanna check if it's maybe undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.81,
          "end": 144.63,
          "en": "so if we used some component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.63,
          "end": 147.03,
          "en": "that uses this hook in the future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.03,
          "end": 148.623,
          "en": "outside of an AccordionItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.67000000000002,
          "end": 152.215,
          "en": "so not wrapped by such an AccordionItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.215,
          "end": 153.573,
          "en": "which would not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.59,
          "end": 157.68,
          "en": "So, we wanna check if the context is maybe not defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.68,
          "end": 160.86,
          "en": "and in that case, I want to throw a new Error again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.86,
          "end": 163.11,
          "en": "to make sure that we're not doing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.11,
          "end": 164.971,
          "en": "where I wanna say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.971,
          "end": 169.5,
          "en": "AccordionItem-related components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.5,
          "end": 174.5,
          "en": "must be wrapped by Accordion.Item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.26,
          "end": 176.09300000000002,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.21,
          "end": 180.9,
          "en": "Well, and now we can go to the AccordionTitle component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.9,
          "end": 183.99,
          "en": "and remove that id prop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.99,
          "end": 188.25,
          "en": "and instead use the AccordionItemContext,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.25,
          "end": 190.32,
          "en": "which we just added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.32,
          "end": 194.7,
          "en": "imported from the AccordionItem.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 194.7,
          "end": 198.333,
          "en": "to get the id of the item this title belongs to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.1,
          "end": 203.46,
          "en": "And we can do exactly the same in AccordionContent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.46,
          "end": 205.98,
          "en": "Get rid of the id prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.98,
          "end": 210.32999999999998,
          "en": "use our custom AccordionItemContext function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.32999999999998,
          "end": 211.77,
          "en": "our custom hook here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.77,
          "end": 212.883,
          "en": "and get the id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.25,
          "end": 219.45,
          "en": "And with all that, back in App.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.45,
          "end": 223.32,
          "en": "we can indeed remove the id from title and content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.32,
          "end": 228,
          "en": "and instead, only add it on the AccordionItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228,
          "end": 229.62,
          "en": "here for the local guides",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 229.62,
          "end": 234.42000000000002,
          "en": "and also here for the experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.42000000000002,
          "end": 238.59,
          "en": "So, remove this id from title and content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.59,
          "end": 240.753,
          "en": "and instead add it to the item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 241.92,
          "end": 243.36,
          "en": "And with that done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 243.36,
          "end": 245.58,
          "en": "if you save everything and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.58,
          "end": 250.14,
          "en": "this still works as before without any errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 250.14,
          "end": 252.84,
          "en": "but now with a better developer experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.84,
          "end": 255.42,
          "en": "where we only have to set the id once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.42,
          "end": 257.22,
          "en": "and it will, behind the scenes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.22,
          "end": 260.733,
          "en": "be consumed by all the components that need that id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 261.57,
          "end": 263.25,
          "en": "Now, we're pretty much done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.25,
          "end": 266.04,
          "en": "with this compound components pattern here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.04,
          "end": 269.37,
          "en": "and there is just one last potential improvement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 269.37,
          "end": 270.57,
          "en": "I want to implement here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.57,
          "end": 272.13,
          "en": "Something you don't have to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 272.13,
          "end": 274.17,
          "en": "but something I want to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.17,
          "end": 276.42,
          "en": "Because at the moment we are, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 276.42,
          "end": 278.94,
          "en": "grouping all those Accordion components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.94,
          "end": 281.31,
          "en": "into that Accordion function object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 281.31,
          "end": 283.86,
          "en": "And that's great because that makes it very clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 283.86,
          "end": 285.6,
          "en": "that these components are meant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.6,
          "end": 288.72,
          "en": "to be used in conjunction with Accordion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.72,
          "end": 289.89,
          "en": "But at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 289.89,
          "end": 293.07,
          "en": "it's also theoretically possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 293.07,
          "end": 297.843,
          "en": "to import AccordionTitle like this and use it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 299.52,
          "end": 301.623,
          "en": "And then, it might not be that clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.623,
          "end": 304.2,
          "en": "that it should be inside of an Accordion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 304.2,
          "end": 306.48,
          "en": "Now, you could say that it is clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 306.48,
          "end": 308.19,
          "en": "and you could of course also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 308.19,
          "end": 311.04,
          "en": "be the only developer working on this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 311.04,
          "end": 313.35,
          "en": "in which case it's clear to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 313.35,
          "end": 316.05,
          "en": "But if you wanna be super safe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 316.05,
          "end": 319.08,
          "en": "that those components never get used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 319.08,
          "end": 321.693,
          "en": "outside of the Accordion context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 322.65,
          "end": 325.92,
          "en": "or if you want to at least make it as clear as possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 325.92,
          "end": 328.29,
          "en": "that they should be used in conjunction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 328.29,
          "end": 331.72,
          "en": "you could of course grab all those components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 332.67,
          "end": 335.82,
          "en": "and merge them all into one single file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 335.82,
          "end": 338.04,
          "en": "so that you don't have to export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 338.04,
          "end": 340.683,
          "en": "those individual Accordion components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 341.7,
          "end": 343.2,
          "en": "I won't do that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 343.2,
          "end": 345.42,
          "en": "because I wanna keep that code separated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 345.42,
          "end": 349.023,
          "en": "to make it as easy to read and understand as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 349.95,
          "end": 351.84000000000003,
          "en": "But I wanted to mention this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.84000000000003,
          "end": 354.27,
          "en": "that this is something you could do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 354.27,
          "end": 355.74,
          "en": "if you want to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 355.74,
          "end": 358.74,
          "en": "that those components can only be accessed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 358.74,
          "end": 361.47,
          "en": "through the Accordion component function object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 361.47,
          "end": 363.33,
          "en": "and not on their own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 363.33,
          "end": 364.983,
          "en": "Here, I'll not do it though.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}